            lines {
              text: "  - Display Font: `Anton` (condensed architectural uppercase for hero headlines)."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - Body Font: `Manrope` (highly legible geometric neo-grotesque for editorial copy)."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - Accent / Script: `Caveat` (tasteful handwritten notes for human annotations and creative callouts)."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "---"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "## 3. Key Product Decisions & Trade-Offs"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 1: Modular Configuration in `site.ts`**"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: All personal details, project data, skills, links, and contact configs live in a centralized typed configuration file (`src/config/site.ts`)."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Aligns with the master prompt specification (Section 2 & 6). The owner can edit personal info in one spot without touching UI components."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 2: Interactive Sandbox & Live Prototype Simulators in Case Studies**"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Case study modals include interactive state simulators (e.g. dynamic color token swapper, responsive component tester, interactive micro-interaction showcase) alongside high-fidelity case study images."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Elevates the portfolio from a static picture gallery to a genuine proof of creative frontend and UX prowess."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 3: Standalone Antigravity Canvas with Global Motion Switch**"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Lightweight HTML5 Canvas particle swarm system configured with velocity physics and mouse gravitation. A persistent `Motion: On/Off` switch in the header allows visitors to pause or disable canvas rendering instantly, with automatic sync to `prefers-reduced-motion`."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Delivers the requested visual flair without degrading CPU/battery performance or violating accessibility standards."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "---"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
