    thinking: "**Reviewing Image Outputs**\n\nI\'ve just reviewed the generated image outputs. So far, the system has provided images named `/src/assets/images/design_system_preview_1794041725106.jpg`, `/src/assets/images/fintech_app_preview_1794041724777.jpg`, and `/src/assets/images/ai_workspace_preview_17940`. I\'m going through each to gauge its relevance.\n\n\n**Verifying Tailwind Configuration**\n\nI\'m now diving into the Tailwind configuration. I\'ve confirmed that the `@theme` block functions as expected in Tailwind v4 with `@tailwindcss/vite` v4, generating the specified custom font families like `font-display`, `font-sans`, and `font-script`. Next, I\'ll be verifying custom scrollbars, noise or glow utilities, and reduced-motion handling to ensure the design system is fully implemented. After that, I will be starting ultra-mode and focus on \"Fast-Feedback Unit Tests\".\n\n\n**Structuring Core Logic**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the project\'s core logic into dedicated utility modules. I\'m focusing on creating a `src/utils/portfolio.ts` module with functions for project filtering, form validation, metric formatting, and even an antigravity swarm physics helper. I\'m also planning to create a `src/utils/portfolio.test.ts` file to test these utilities using Node\'s test runner, ensuring they\'re functioning correctly. I\'m now developing the site data in `src/config/site.ts`.\n\n\n**Defining Portfolio Details**\n\nI\'m now defining the portfolio details. I\'ve populated my email, portrait, and resume link. I\'ve also verified key stats and metrics, and am constructing a projects array with cover images, descriptions, prototype specs, design tokens, problem/solution, testimonials, and tools used. I\'m breaking down my skills and tools, and structuring the 6-step human design process. Finally, I\'m documenting my experience timeline.\n\n\n**Outlining Component Architecture**\n\nI\'m now outlining the component architecture. I\'m focusing on key components like `Hero.tsx` for the introductory section with typography and call-to-action buttons. I\'m also planning `ProjectGrid.tsx` for interactive filtering, `ProjectDialog.tsx` as a case study viewer, and `ProcessAndSkills.tsx` to showcase the design process. I will also be working on `AntigravityCanvas.tsx`, for interactive effects, `ContactSection.tsx` for inquiries, and the `Footer.tsx` for key site information, and integrating the components in the `App.tsx` file, including state management and modals.\n\n\n"
