    thinking: "**Examining Component Icons**\n\nI\'m currently looking at the icons available within `lucide-react` for use in `Header.tsx`. I\'ve identified `Sparkles`, `Menu`, `X`, `ArrowUpRight`, `Play`, `Pause`, `Power`, and `Activity`. Now, I\'m constructing an enhanced toggle switch, specifically a \"Stylized Prominent Motion Switch\" in `Header.tsx`.\n\n\n**Constructing Prominent Switch**\n\nI\'ve just finished the \"Stylized Prominent Motion Switch\" component within `Header.tsx`. It now incorporates a visual switch, complete with dynamic styling, an accessible `role=\"switch\"`, `aria-checked` attributes, hover states, and focus-visible outlines. The switch indicates state visually with text, and color, along with a particle swarm effect.\n\n\n**Refining Visual States**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual states of the toggle switch. The focus is on the text and track/thumb components. I\'ve introduced a subtle pulse effect to the thumb when active and a line-through on the \"PAUSED\" state text when the toggle is off. I\'ve also adjusted the color palette for a clearer visual indication.\n\n\n"
