    thinking: "**Analyzing Chatbot\'s Design**\n\nI\'ve made a key discovery: the `metadata.json` file already lists `\"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]`. This is significant! Now, the focus is the chatbot\'s design and role. The user wants the chatbot\'s theme to align with the overall project aesthetic.\n\n\n**Defining Chatbot\'s Persona**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the chatbot\'s persona. The feature block dictates its function as Saiful\'s interactive AI design concierge and system copilot. The system instruction specifies deep knowledge of Saiful\'s background, skills, and projects. I\'ve got the role description solidified; Saiful AI should have a confident, technical, and design-literate tone, matching the cinematic noir aesthetic.\n\n\n**Refining UI Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now diving into the UI details, starting with color schemes and typography. I\'ve pinned down the core color palette to `#121212`, `#171717`, `#262626`, `#e32b3c`, and `#f2efeb`. Typography will use Anton for headings and Manrope for body text, with monospace uppercase micro-labels. Key design elements will use zero-pill discipline with no tacky buttons and geometric borders to maintain the noir theme.\n\n\n**Developing Server-Side Implementation**\n\nI\'m now switching gears to the server implementation. I\'ve begun creating `server.ts` and identifying required packages: `express`, `dotenv`, `@google/genai`, `path`, and either `fileURLToPath` or `process.cwd()`. I\'m going with ES modules, given the `package.json` setup. I\'ve got the import statements ready for the critical modules.\n\n\n**Implementing Gemini API Call**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Gemini API call using `@google/genai`. I\'ve reviewed the call pattern from `SKILL.md` and the package documentation. The input messages will be formatted into a consistent structure for the `generateContent` method. I\'ve also verified how to handle multi-turn chats, ensuring proper role mapping.\n\n\n**Verifying System Instructions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION`. It needs to contain comprehensive details about Saiful Islam, including his identity as a UI/UX designer and creative frontend engineer, his specialities in design systems and creative frontend, and also his design philosophy, all of which are critical for the chatbot\'s knowledge base. I\'m aiming for a detailed, yet concise, instruction. The instruction will have to be stateless, per request.\n\n\n**Crafting Chatbot Context**\n\nI\'m now integrating the project details to inform the chatbot\'s knowledge. I\'m focusing on key data points like the enterprise token library adoption rate, App Store rating, tech used, and project pricing. This information will give the bot specific knowledge about the creator and associated projects. The aim is to make the bot very informed.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_11031867464842720343"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"/**\\n * @license\\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\\n */\\n\\nimport express from \'express\';\\nimport { createServer as createViteServer } from \'vite\';\\nimport path from \'path\';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \'url\';\\nimport dotenv from \'dotenv\';\\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \'@google/genai\';\\n\\ndotenv.config();\\n\\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\\n\\nconst app = express();\\nconst port = parseInt(process.env.PORT || \'3000\', 10);\\n\\napp.use(express.json());\\n\\n// Initialize server-side Gemini client\\nconst ai = new GoogleGenAI({\\n  apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY,\\n  httpOptions: {\\n    headers: {\\n      \'User-Agent\': \'aistudio-build\',\\n    },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\nconst SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION = `You are Saiful Islam\'s AI Design Copilot & Studio Concierge on his official portfolio website.\\nSaiful Islam is an accomplished UI/UX Designer & Creative Frontend Engineer based in Dhaka, Bangladesh, available worldwide for contracts, design systems architecture, and interactive prototyping.\\n\\nYOUR ROLES & CAPABILITIES:\\n1. Provide accurate, thoughtful, and articulate information regarding Saiful\'s work, engineering methodology, design token philosophy, and featured projects.\\n2. Answer inquiries about project pricing, timelines, deliverables, and collaboration models with clarity.\\n3. Help visitors and potential clients formulate a project brief or discuss design engineering challenges.\\n4. Maintain a sleek, design-literate, professional, and confident persona that reflects Saiful\'s \\\"Cinematic Noir\\\" aesthetic (clean, concise, brutally authentic, and zero-fluff).\\n\\nKEY PORTFOLIO KNOWLEDGE BASE:\\n- Full Name: Saiful Islam\\n- Title: UI/UX Designer & Creative Frontend Engineer\\n- Experience: 6+ years shipping 40+ products, 14 enterprise design systems, 99.4% token adoption.\\n- Core Stack: Figma (Variables, Auto-Layout, Components), React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, Framer Motion, HTML5 Canvas & WebGL, W3C Design Tokens, Node.js.\\n- Three Design Invariants:\\n  1. Zero Handoff Ambiguity: Designers and engineers speak the exact same token language; components and code are synchronized.\\n  2. Sensory Micro-Interactions: Fluid gesture springs, physical hover dynamics, and tactile sound/motion make software feel alive.\\n  3. Accessible Without Compromise: Strict WCAG AA/AAA compliance, 4.5:1+ contrast ratios, keyboard focus traps, and reduced-motion support.\\n\\nFEATURED PROJECTS:\\n- \\\"Aurora Design System v1.2\\\" (2025): Multi-brand enterprise token architecture with React/Tailwind synchronization for Global FinTech Consortium.\\n- \\\"Aura Mobile Banking & Crypto\\\" (2024): Tactile mobile banking experience with fluid gesture physics and biometric security.\\n- \\\"Synergy Creative AI Workspace\\\" (2025): Node-graph spatial canvas for generative design workflows in React 19.\\n- \\\"Aethel Luxury Catalog\\\" (2024): Editorial digital monograph emphasizing typographic hierarchy and architectural curation.\\n- \\\"Nexus Token CLI & Studio\\\" (2025): Open-source utility compiling Figma Variables directly into CSS tokens and TypeScript types.\\n- \\\"Chronos Tactile Stopwatch\\\" (2024): Keyboard-driven analog focus timer with synthesized audio feedback.\\n\\nPRICING & SCOPE TIERS:\\n- \\\"Design System Sprint\\\" ($1,850 flat fee, 2-3 weeks): Complete token architecture in Figma & React (25+ WCAG AAA components, token dictionary, documentation).\\n- \\\"Product & Interactive Prototype\\\" ($3,400 flat fee, 4-6 weeks): Full UX research, up to 15 hi-fi views, and a production-grade React prototype with micro-interaction physics.\\n- \\\"Design Engineering Retainer\\\" ($2,400/month, dedicated partnership): 20 hours/week dedicated design & code capacity, direct Slack/GitHub team integration, priority turnaround.\\n\\nCONTACT CHANNELS:\\n- Primary Email: zen.saifulhere@gmail.com\\n- LinkedIn: https://linkedin.com/in/saifulhere\\n- GitHub: https://github.com/sifulabdullah\\n\\nGUIDELINES FOR YOUR RESPONSES:\\n- Format responses cleanly with brief paragraphs and bullet points when listing specs or deliverables.\\n- Keep answers concise, helpful, and focused on design/code substance.\\n- Encourage visitors to book a sprint, schedule a conversation, or reach out at zen.saifulhere@gmail.com.\\n`;\\n\\n// POST /api/chat - Multi-turn conversational endpoint\\napp.post(\'/api/chat\', async (req, res) => {\\n  try {\\n    const { messages, model = \'gemini-3.8-flash\' } = req.body;\\n\\n    if (!Array.isArray(messages) || messages.length === 0) {\\n      return res.status(400).json({ error: \'Messages array is required.\' });\\n    }\\n\\n    // Supported models based on the task speed and complexity\\n    const validModels = [\'gemini-3.8-flash\', \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\', \'gemini-4-argon\'];\\n    const selectedModel = validModels.includes(model) ? model : \'gemini-3.8-flash\';\\n\\n    // Format multi-turn conversation for @google/genai SDK\\n    const contents = messages.map((m: { role: string; content: string }) => ({\\n      role: m.role === \'assistant\' || m.role === \'model\' ? \'model\' : \'user\',\\n      parts: [{ text: m.content }],\\n    }));\\n\\n    const response = await ai.models.generateContent({\\n      model: selectedModel,\\n      contents,\\n      config: {\\n        systemInstruction: SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION,\\n      },\\n    });\\n\\n    const replyText = response.text || \\\"I\'m here to assist with Saiful\'s portfolio, design systems, and frontend engineering inquiries. How can I help you today?\\\";\\n\\n    return res.json({\\n      text: replyText,\\n      modelUsed: selectedModel,\\n    });\\n  } catch (error: any) {\\n    console.error(\'Gemini API Error in /api/chat:\', error);\\n    const errorMessage = error?.message || \'An error occurred while contacting the AI design concierge.\';\\n    return res.status(500).json({ error: errorMessage });\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nasync function startServer() {\\n  const isProduction = process.env.NODE_ENV === \'production\';\\n\\n  if (!isProduction) {\\n    const vite = await createViteServer({\\n      server: { middlewareMode: true },\\n      appType: \'spa\',\\n    });\\n    app.use(vite.middlewares);\\n  } else {\\n    app.use(express.static(path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\')));\\n    app.get(\'*\', (_req, res) => {\\n      res.sendFile(path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\', \'index.html\'));\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  app.listen(port, \'0.0.0.0\', () => {\\n    console.log(`Portfolio server with Gemini AI copilot running on http://localhost:${port}`);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nstartServer();\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create server.ts with Express, Vite dev middleware, and Gemini server-side /api/chat route\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/server.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing server.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create Express server with Gemini chat route\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\227?\n\224?\001i\024}\023#\257l\340\341G!W\202T\220&K\345I\002\030(\022\266k;\002\021k\300o\233\314\246L\3600\354\332=Q\2674\'\\d\346\331\002\236\242\266\304\236\371\311S?J\034\232\0335\334\b\244\"\222\v\276\244R\001\322\220(A\t\266\372\273\337;\352\311\b\356\317<\327\364/\2551aA\364\'\rn\3014ngO\352\034\377\336\000\301\312\0376\314T\026\351\275\211\227\244jN\016~\337\'\222\311=[\205\361\231*Me\351a\324V\243\226\333{\204\3257N\"\353\225!\222\215\220!\024|\370\254\343k\n\031\242\0023\342x\333\v\276\335*)Y<|\210\277\216\322\261\360\036N\362\332\240c\216\024\223;\307\345\024\244\333\253\232j<H\307\276\016\316fu\221#\202\213\373\325\032\375\361\365\'x\243\036y\240\221PDX\245\373h\006\354\344C\026\303l\023\3565\250i\273\321\365\345\371k\344Kv|-\275F3)\310\220\201\262D\221\334\365\334\037\302\315y\332\305\202\357\373\3252X\315\'\316\026\214aq|\256!\357\307\207\340Y\320\\s\345\371zuT\356\250\030zV\272\024 \266\236\201Pg\276\277\005L\343\003b\264\235\\\317\254\213@l\355\001\221\360\027\335^n\236=5<\033\n\177\215[\276\257Q\317\354\'^;.\236 )\242>\246\202\316\353a/\201\303\311\276 \232f\177\243\227T\366\271\307\260ad\200\332Z\241\332P\227\333\245\343Q\376\0316gSd\025OB\233P\352\340X\226\t\315\224\37608\264:#\202\366_\205a\343\212\017\226\244\212\253\322\3528\240\215N\244\223\202\207\216\331\300\b\233\251\'\t_\f\367\001S)\362\351C\354\205h\301\231\341\334\360\000\354\004PD\341S7m\036\260\004L\303\334\255q\215\245\267.\335\266?6\367\034\255u\376\020\224\033\2243]w\341\006\271t\202\315p\205\005\3473\260P\322\211<\237\337\256p\365\224:1\032\205\375\241IqX\210$\367V\247\244\004\364\375\023\366&\214\277p\354\311\340\004\202\300\245\261-K\300\334\241f\377\360\357\\rw\262\"\367\353_C~\332\214\231\353C\331\227\354\017CD\022\273\n1\350\373r\031\223j\311Zm\261\325\035\307\276\025\261U\225\370\033,BY\003\024ix\270{\303+\204\002\234\0044L\005\205~\354\364$\361\336\000wC\324\302\316\203\365F\335\336a`dP\373\3471W\277\021\257\225T{\355Sz\371\316\270W,v\311\27