    thinking: "**Designing the Chatbot**\n\nI\'m now diving into the client-side chatbot component, specifically `src/components/StudioChatbot.tsx`. My current focus is integrating the \"Cinematic Noir\" aesthetic from Saiful Islam\'s portfolio. I\'m prioritizing the color palette: an obsidian background and deep charcoal surfaces to set the mood. I\'ll need to consider typography choices to complement the color scheme.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Elements**\n\nI\'ve finalized the UI components\' visual aspects. I\'ve settled on the color palette, focusing on obsidian, charcoal, and crimson hues, complemented by warm off-white and muted secondary text. For typography, I\'ve chosen Anton for display, Manrope for the body, and uppercase tracked monospace for labels. I\'m maintaining a strict \"Zero-Pill\" discipline, prioritizing rectangular geometric elements. I\'ve also integrated unboxed status indicators with subtle dividers.\n\n\n**Defining Chatbot Interactions**\n\nI\'m now outlining the chatbot\'s interactive elements, starting with a welcome card featuring Saiful\'s persona. I\'ll include quick starter prompts to encourage user engagement, like questions about the Sprint, design tokens, and prototypes. Message bubbles will have sleek, distinct designs for user and AI responses, including markdown formatting and copy options. I\'m planning a crimson typing indicator and an error banner with a retry function. Finally, the input bar will have a monospace prompt placeholder and a \"Send\" button with a disclaimer about Gemini.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_10981329947284685251"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"/**\\n * @license\\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\\n */\\n\\nexport interface ChatMessage {\\n  id: string;\\n  role: \'user\' | \'assistant\';\\n  content: string;\\n  timestamp: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface SuggestedPrompt {\\n  id: string;\\n  label: string;\\n  prompt: string;\\n  category: \'pricing\' | \'engineering\' | \'projects\' | \'process\';\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateChatMessage(text: string): { isValid: boolean; error?: string } {\\n  const trimmed = text.trim();\\n  if (!trimmed) {\\n    return { isValid: false, error: \'Message cannot be empty.\' };\\n  }\\n  if (trimmed.length > 2000) {\\n    return { isValid: false, error: \'Message exceeds 2,000 character limit.\' };\\n  }\\n  return { isValid: true };\\n}\\n\\nexport function createChatMessage(\\n  role: \'user\' | \'assistant\',\\n  content: string\\n): ChatMessage {\\n  const now = new Date();\\n  const timeStr = now.toLocaleTimeString([], { hour: \'2-digit\', minute: \'2-digit\' });\\n  return {\\n    id: `msg-${Date.now()}-${Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 7)}`,\\n    role,\\n    content: content.trim(),\\n    timestamp: timeStr,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport const SUGGESTED_PROMPTS: SuggestedPrompt[] = [\\n  {\\n    id: \'p-1\',\\n    label: \'$1,850 Sprint Scope\',\\n    prompt: \'What deliverables are included in the $1,850 Design System Sprint?\',\\n    category: \'pricing\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'p-2\',\\n    label: \'Design Invariants\',\\n    prompt: \'What are Saiful\\\\\'s three core design invariants and how do they shape his code?\',\\n    category: \'process\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'p-3\',\\n    label: \'Interactive Prototypes\',\\n    prompt: \'How does Saiful turn Figma prototypes into production React & Framer Motion applications?\',\\n    category: \'engineering\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'p-4\',\\n    label: \'Aurora Design System\',\\n    prompt: \'Tell me about the Aurora Design System v1.2 case study and token architecture.\',\\n    category: \'projects\',\\n  },\\n];\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create chat utilities and message validation logic\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/chat.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing chat utilities\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create chat utilities\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\332\031\n\327\031\001i\024}\023\274\274\016\264f\322\327\b\265\\\374\254RXq>m\304(4A5]\004\274\377\352\270\347+[c*\256\222V\337\235\177s&\344\253\211P\273\320\303\266\307q\240wX \265\323\372\263\365\260\206`\217\263\330\227\361\364\215\020p\220w\2062\t\251h\036W\2232]f\247s\201%\002\346R\202\356\2170q\235\f\340/T\022\371\205\254\270\271z\363Fe\374j3\337\354\356|Nd\362\336\252V\310v.\211\207qa\327!?`\353xD\241\257o1\004\221\247A\341\277\353\3512\r\257\224r\275O\225\251N\274\370\351z\237\024Q\004,\n\205\244\3435\3744\2400\311\371\020\303Q\337Gi\367\210;\215\236>\020\326?\263\004\004\217a\334$\330h%\t\r\n\"\270y\246\306\222\313\202\205\263\243\233\323P\267iG\221y8\217\026\256\314uY\235pR\250\300\352\352\202\250\273S\272\006\363\237\245\200\337\262\325\210k]\211!x\235u\317It9\325\032\2703\244\257\034\362o\353,\216X\a\231\350|s\310\272\356\024\331\323\212|\300Y\276\244\302\252X\314\235\232J\257\332\020v[$\005\316\225\356\210\216\b\177t\350\016\306\372<\2777\303\255\254>k\022\237\317\372\361M\210\276D\255im\035\t;d\352D\374\203?\225\234&H\200\006)J\263\203\245;!\257\265\b@\207h\365\004%V\303\261iJI\376\314\260\357\b\211\030\226\3049\247\301\036\374\317(\210Q3\226\260Qh\374G0\001\237\223\205,S~\363\203:\341\035]\\\370P\270r6~\232\254\367\277\207\337?\213\216\361\316\207\355\v\332Q\335N\320\331L\323\305\027\267\262\375M\201\301i\347T]\217\3268\365\\\272[K\241c7f\377JD\fv\235T\215Z\237\206\246U\252;\240\231\037\250\260Tf\303\245iE\3103\324C9\223Y\331U\215\301\326\221\213-A\312\316\347\341\2327o\355\366\177\377\"\241 \r\000\233\266u\277\272J\0160\274\034\204\371Z~\364~,\\\316\215T\277\377+\237\263\373\026\220\270\215\023f7\bf\305\335+\352\254\232e\022\326\360\316\325\fI\312\254XF\277\215x\035\223N\256\242\3417~\265\271\002\321\341\275_b].\255\350\301\220\3053\035p\250\a\341\223\234=\a\237-\372\027\316\304\336\024{\332Z2\354\333\353\314%\3667PDF\224G\rd\001\215\256:\256\034\177K\233\323\336\370#\252\250\267cMO\246\b$\001\210~\037yx_\323\372vv\00