    response: "The chatbot has been implemented and styled to match the **Cinematic Noir** design language of Saiful Islam\'s portfolio:\n\n### Key Design & Functional Highlights\n\n1. **Aesthetic & Visual Match with Cinematic Noir**:\n   - **Obsidian Palette & Hairline Accents**: Deep `#090909` and `#111111` backdrop surfaces with subtle `#262626` hairline borders and `#e32b3c` crimson focus rings.\n   - **Zero-Pill Geometric Discipline**: Clean unboxed headers, rectangular geometry, and monospace metadata tags (`ONLINE \302\267 GEMINI 3.8 FLASH`) separated by `\302\267` and `/` dividers.\n   - **Floating Dock Controller**: Bottom-right floating trigger with an active crimson beacon, animated pulse, and quick expand/collapse toggle.\n\n2. **Full-Stack Gemini Architecture**:\n   - **Server-Side API (`/api/chat` in `server.ts`)**: Built with Express and the official `@google/genai` TypeScript SDK. The Gemini API key is kept secure on the server side (`process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`).\n   - **Model Speed & Task Toggle**: Fast toggling between **Gemini 3.8 Flash** (general high-intelligence reasoning) and **Gemini 3.1 Flash Lite** (ultra-low latency responses).\n   - **Studio Knowledge Context**: System instructions encode Saiful Islam\342\200\231s professional profile, tech stack (React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind v4, Figma Variables), featured case studies (Aurora Design System, Aura Mobile Banking), three design invariants, transparent rates ($1,850 Sprint, $3,400 Flagship, $2,400 Retainer), and direct contact channels (`zen.saifulhere@gmail.com`).\n\n3. **Multi-Turn Chat Experience**:\n   - **Scrollable Conversation Thread**: Message bubbles with copy-to-clipboard actions, timestamps, and markdown formatting.\n   - **Interactive Starter Chips**: Quick suggestion inquiries for instant exploration of sprint scope, invariants, React prototypes, and design systems.\n   - **Keyboard First**: Direct `[Enter]` to dispatch and `[Shift + Enter]` for multiline inputs.\n\n4. **Verification & Quality**:\n   - All 6 unit tests (`portfolio.test.ts`) passing cleanly.\n   - TypeScript compiles and lints with 0 errors (`tsc --noEmit`).\n   - Browser interaction verified with active query dispatch and response rendering."
