  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s request. It seems they want to replace \"SAIFUL ISLAM\" with \"saifulhere\" in either the header brand link or the hero heading. I\'m investigating the header brand, currently \"SAIFUL ISLAM / UI\302\267UX ENG\", and comparing the use case of both potential target elements.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Intent**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user\'s explicit request regarding the header. It seems they want \"SAIFUL ISLAM\" changed to \"saifulhere\" in the header navigation, which they call the \"heading.\" I\'ll need to check `Header.tsx` to implement this. Furthermore, I\'ll assess whether \"saifulhere\" should also replace \"Saiful Islam\" in the hero heading.\n\nI\'m also working on the chatbot. The focus is to rename it to \"Saiful\'s AI\" and optimize its presentation for different devices. Specifically, I\'m considering a full-screen or bottom-sheet design for mobile screens.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile Responsiveness**\n\nI\'m now focusing on mobile optimizations. I\'m prioritizing the chatbot\'s mobile presentation, exploring full-screen, bottom-sheet, and responsive drawer designs. I also need to ensure responsive font sizes and proper keyboard handling for a better user experience. Furthermore, I\'ll integrate a \"Services\" tab into the header navigation, linking to the relevant section on the page. Finally, I\'m working on header responsiveness, specifically the mobile navigation menu.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Mobile Optimization**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into mobile responsiveness across various sections. I\'m focusing on the hero section\'s portrait image, ensuring proper sizing and aspect ratio, especially on smaller screens, and centering the stacking on mobile. The project grid\'s responsive columns and touch-friendly cards are being addressed, along with horizontal scrollable tabs. The pricing section\'s stacking cards and clear typography are also priorities. The contact form\'s 16px minimum font size is being applied for iOS Safari and I\'m ensuring a clean responsive header reflow for the Swarm toggle and \"Let\'s Talk\" button. I\'ll also modify their shape to align with the sharp, rectangular geometry of the build.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now focused on refining visual elements. I\'m replacing the rounded Swarm toggle with a precise rectangular module featuring a dark chassis and crimson glow. The \"Let\'s Talk\" button is also getting a sharp rectangular design, cinematic crimson accent, and diagonal arrow icon. Additionally, I\'ll add more tools I use, giving them a frosted glass background with a low red accent. Specifically, I\'m updating `ProcessAndSkills.tsx` and `site.ts` to include Figma, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, Next.js, Framer Motion, WebGL / Three.js, HTML5 Canvas API, VS Code, Git / GitHub, Postman, and Storybook.\n\n\n"
