  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Expanding the Tools List**\n\nI\'m now expanding the tools list based on the user\'s request. Focusing on industry-standard design and prototyping software, I\'ve added Figma, Framer, and Fig to the initial list. My next step will be to explore and categorize the additional tools needed for a senior UI/UX designer and a creative frontend engineer, ensuring a comprehensive toolkit is established for the user.\n\n\n**Categorizing Further Toolsets**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into specialized toolsets. I\'ve categorized tools for frontend engineering and creative coding. I\'m focusing on languages and frameworks like React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Next.js, and animation libraries. I\'m also addressing token infrastructure with tools like Style Dictionary and W3C Design Tokens, plus the required design. I\'m also adding in the visual design elements, giving them a frosted glass background with a low red accent, and have created the necessary code and design to make this.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual design, incorporating a \"frosted glass\" effect using `hover:text-white transition-colors` to create a luxurious and tactile feel. I\'m focusing on the Cinematic Noir aesthetic, and integrating a subtle low red glow. I\'ve got the design code ready and in place.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Optimizing Chatbot**\n\nI\'m now implementing the chatbot optimization and renaming. I\'m updating `StudioChatbot.tsx` and focusing on the renaming tasks. I\'ve changed the names of the floating button, terminal header, assistant message sender, welcome greeting, and system prompts to \"Saiful\'s AI.\" I\'ve updated both the names, and their associated code. I\'m also implementing device optimization. I\'m going to ensure the chatbot adjusts to mobile screens (width, bottom sheet feel with swipe/drag handle, responsive font sizes).\n\n\n**Implementing Mobile Refinements**\n\nI\'m now implementing mobile enhancements. I\'ve focused on input auto-zoom adjustments and touch-scrolling optimization. I\'ve also implemented a sleek compact floating trigger button for easy access on mobile, ensuring it doesn\'t overlap content. Furthermore, I\'ve implemented a easily tappable close button with minimum 44px touch target on mobile!\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m now making modifications to the header and hero sections. I\'m updating the brand heading to \"SAIFULHERE\" with a sublabel. In the hero section, I\'ve updated the H1 headline to \"SAIFULHERE\" and integrated an updated subtext with a verified profile badge. Finally, I\'ve also added \"Services\" to the header\'s desktop nav.\n\n\n**Refining Nav and IDs**\n\nI\'m now integrating new navigation elements and IDs. I\'ve updated both the desktop and mobile menus, assigning specific anchor links. I\'ve also implemented `id=\"services\"` within `ProcessAndSkills.tsx` to provide direct access to the services matrix upon clicking the corresponding link.\n\n**Optimizing Visuals**\n\nI\'m now updating the UI with precise, rectilinear designs. I\'m focusing on the \"swarm toggle\" and \"Let\'s Talk\" button, and have decided to remove the rounded shapes, and switch to a more sharp-edged and micro-radius rectangular style, in keeping with the build\'s overall aesthetic.\n\n\n**Crafting Button Designs**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the visual language through the toggle module and \"Let\'s Talk\" button. I\'m prioritizing a clean, modern aesthetic with a precision-machined cinematic rectangular toggle module design, complete with a sharp rectangular geometry for the \"Let\'s Talk\" button, and have specified precise code details to realize the design elements. I\'m going for the desired aesthetic through carefully-defined styling attributes.\n\n\n**Implementing Mobile Design**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in mobile device optimization. I\'m focusing on responsiveness across all sections. I\'ve ensured a clean alignment within the header, and implemented a full-width mobile menu with a backdrop blur and large touch targets. Furthermore, I\'ve ensured the hero section adapts responsively to mobile screens. I\'ve also implemented horizontal scrolling for category filter tabs in the project grid, and am ensuring the pricing tabs adapt to mobile.\n\n\n"
