    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Requests**:\n  1. Change the heading brand name from \"SAIFUL ISLAM\" to **`saifulhere`**.\n  2. Optimize the chatbot according to the device (bottom-sheet/native layout on mobile, safe-area insets, prevent auto-zoom). Rename it to **`Saiful\'s AI`**.\n  3. Add a **`Services`** tab in the heading navigation (desktop & mobile drawer) linking to `#services`.\n  4. Optimize the entire website for mobile devices (responsive portrait aspect ratio, scrollable category/pricing tabs, touch-friendly touch targets).\n  5. Give the **swarm toggle** a cinematic, professional rectangular look and style the **\"Let\'s Talk\"** button to match the rest of the build\'s sharp geometry (zero-pill discipline).\n  6. Add **more tools** that Saiful uses and give them a **frosted glass background with a low red accent**.\n- **Identity & Contact Details**:\n  - Full Name: Saiful Islam\n  - Brand/Heading: `saifulhere`\n  - Email: `zen.saifulhere@gmail.com`\n  - LinkedIn: `https://linkedin.com/in/saifulhere`\n  - GitHub: `https://github.com/sifulabdullah`\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed File Edits**:\n  - `/src/config/site.ts`: Expanded `siteConfig.tools` to 16 verified software tools (Figma, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, Next.js, Framer Motion, Framer, WebGL & Three.js, HTML5 Canvas API, Style Dictionary, Storybook, VS Code, Git & GitHub, Node.js & Express, Postman, Docker).\n  - `/src/components/Header.tsx`: Completely updated. Changed brand wordmark to `SAIFULHERE`, added `Services` link in desktop nav and mobile drawer, implemented sharp cinematic rectangular swarm toggle (`[SWARM ON]` / `[SWARM OFF]` with sliding block and indicator beacon), and redesigned `Let\'s Talk` with sharp rectangular geometry, crimson glow, and bold monospace tracking.\n  - `/src/components/Hero.tsx`: Updated H1 headline to `SAIFULHERE`, refined subtitle and verified badge (`Saiful Islam (@saifulhere)`), and optimized mobile portrait container sizing (`max-w-[300px] sm:max-w-sm md:max-w-md`) with flexible button wrapping.\n  - `/src/components/ProcessAndSkills.tsx`: Updated with `id=\"services\"` for navigation anchoring, rendered all 16 tools in a frosted glass grid (`bg-[#141416]/50 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/[0.07]`) with low red ambient background glows (`bg-[#e32b3c]/[0.05]`), low red top-corner accents, and crimson indicator pips.\n  - `/src/components/StudioChatbot.tsx`: Completely updated. Renamed to **Saiful\'s AI** in launcher button, header, and system greetings. Optimized for mobile: acts as an 88vh bottom sheet with drag indicator bar on mobile, smooth touch scrolling, safe-area insets (`pb-safe`), `text-base sm:text-xs` textarea to prevent mobile Safari auto-zoom, and compact floating launcher placement (`bottom-4 right-4 sm:bottom-6 sm:right-6`).\n  - `/src/components/PricingSection.tsx`: Replaced pill-shaped tabs with sharp rectangular tabs, enabled horizontal scroll on mobile with `overflow-x-auto scrollbar-none`.\n  - `/src/components/ProjectGrid.tsx`: Replaced rounded pill category buttons with sharp rectangular monospace buttons with smooth mobile horizontal scroll.\n  - `/server.ts`: Server-side Gemini chat endpoint (`/api/chat`) updated with `Saiful\'s AI` persona and portfolio knowledge fallback.\n  - `/src/utils/portfolio.test.ts`: 6/6 unit tests passing.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **Zero-Pill Geometric Discipline**: Pill-shaped badges and rounded-full toggle tracks clashed with the brutalist \"Cinematic Noir\" aesthetic. Transitioning the swarm toggle into a sharp, precision-machined rectangular carrier and the \"Let\'s Talk\" button into a bold crimson rectangular module with monospace typography created strong visual cohesion.\n- **Mobile Viewport Optimization**: On mobile devices (< 640px), a standard fixed 440px wide modal clips off-screen. Converting `StudioChatbot` into a full-width bottom sheet (`inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-[88vh]`) with a top drag indicator bar provides a seamless mobile experience.\n- **Form Auto-Zoom Prevention**: Inputs with font size under 16px cause iOS Safari to auto-zoom on focus. Setting `text-base sm:text-sm` on input fields prevents this jarring layout shift on mobile while keeping desktop text sharp.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Replace file error on `ContactSection.tsx`**:\n  - *Error*: `replace_file_content: chunk 0: target content not found in file`.\n  - *Cause*: Exact line range / content mismatch in `ContactSection.tsx` for lines 211-275.\n  - *Fix*: Need to read lines 200-290 of `src/components/ContactSection.tsx` with `view_file` to get the exact lines before patching input styles.\n- **Playwright click argument syntax**:\n  - *Error*: `Unknown option: --ref`.\n  - *Fix*: Use `npx playwright-cli click <ref>` directly without `--ref` flag.\n- **Gemini API Key missing in dev environment**:\n  - *Issue*: Missing `GEMINI_API_KEY` in local dev environment caused unbounded HTTP calls.\n  - *Fix*: Implemented an 8-second `Promise.race` timeout on server-side Gemini API calls along with an intelligent studio knowledge fallback generator, ensuring responses are always fast and accurate even without an active key.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Dev Server**: Running on port 3000 via `tsx server.ts`.\n- **Files Partially Pending Polish**:\n  - `src/components/ContactSection.tsx`: Needs inspection to update input font size to `text-base sm:text-sm` and ensure card corners are sharp.\n  - Final verification: Co-execute `compile_applet` + `lint_applet` and run Playwright mobile viewport snapshot (390\303\227844) to inspect mobile reflow, header, tools, and `Saiful\'s AI`.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. **View & Update `src/components/ContactSection.tsx`**:\n   - Call `view_file` on `/src/components/ContactSection.tsx` around lines 200\342\200\223260.\n   - Use `replace_file_content` to apply `text-base sm:text-sm` on inputs (`name`, `email`, `service`, `budget`, `message`) to prevent mobile auto-zoom, and update any `rounded-2xl` / `rounded-lg` containers to sharp `rounded-none`.\n2. **Co-execute Verifications**:\n   - Run `npx --yes tsx --test src/utils/portfolio.test.ts` to ensure all 6 unit tests pass.\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together to verify 0 build and TypeScript lint errors.\n3. **Browser Mobile Visual Inspection via `computer-use`**:\n   - Run Playwright: `npx playwright-cli open http://localhost:3000` with mobile dimensions (e.g. 390\303\227844) or navigate and resize.\n   - Test clicking the new `Services` nav tab in the header.\n   - Take a screenshot of the tools grid to verify the frosted glass background and low red accents.\n   - Open `Saiful\'s AI` on mobile and capture a screenshot of the mobile bottom sheet.\n   - Close browser cleanly (`npx playwright-cli close`).\n4. **Final Response**:\n   - Provide a concise summary to the user outlining the renamed brand `saifulhere`, the new `Services` tab, the rectangular swarm toggle, the frosted glass tools suite, and the device-optimized `Saiful\'s AI`.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Zero-Pill Discipline**: No `rounded-full` pill buttons or static badge chips. All buttons, toggles, and cards must maintain sharp or micro-radius geometry.\n- **Exact Branding**: Header brand wordmark and hero heading must say **`SAIFULHERE`**.\n- **Chatbot Identity**: Chatbot name must strictly be **`Saiful\'s AI`**.\n- **Contact Credentials**: Email remains `zen.saifulhere@gmail.com`, LinkedIn `https://linkedin.com/in/saifulhere`.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 163
    included_step_index_end: 360
