  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Generating Testimonial Data**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the structure for testimonial data. I\'ve started by outlining a `TestimonialItem` interface. It includes fields for ID, quote, author details, and the project the testimonial relates to. I believe this provides a solid foundation for generating diverse and realistic testimonials.\n\n\n**Crafting Compelling Testimonials**\n\nI\'ve been working on fleshing out specific testimonial examples. I\'m focusing on defining impact metrics, like percentage improvements or ratings, to add authenticity. I\'m imagining testimonials from Elena Rostova at Consortium FinTech, and Marcus Sterling from Aura Capital. I want to ensure each is tied to Saiful\'s portfolio and provides a realistic, high-impact quote. I\'m prioritizing verifiable data points.\n\n\n**Refining Testimonial Detail**\n\nI\'ve added data for 2 more testimonials. I\'ve included Dr. Sophia Chen from Synergy Studio, highlighting Saiful\'s work on their node-graph canvas and impact on 60 FPS WebGL. Also, Arthur Pendelton from Aethel Atelier praises Saiful\'s cinematic eye and attention to detail. I\'m focusing on ensuring each quote is credible and represents tangible value.\n\n\n**Adding New Testimonial**\n\nI\'ve just generated a new testimonial from Kareem Al-Mansoor at Apex Digital. I\'ve focused on quantifiable impact\342\200\224specifically, zero token drift across 140+ screens\342\200\224to provide a solid reference. I\'ve highlighted Saiful\'s technical fluency in different areas, which makes the quote credible, and provides a compelling, positive impact metric. I\'ll make sure it\'s usable in the component.\n\n\n\n**Designing Testimonial Presentation**\n\nI\'m now focused on the visual presentation of the testimonials. I\'m exploring a design centered around a sharp, zero-pill geometric aesthetic. It\'s built around a monospace index marker, large quotation marks, and a high-impact badge with precise data. I\'m incorporating client avatars and detailed info blocks, plus verified indicators. The carousel controls will be integrated to ensure intuitive navigation.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Controls**\n\nI\'m now integrating interactive carousel controls. I\'m focusing on sharp, rectangular buttons with arrow icons for navigation, as well as a monospace slide counter with a progress bar or stepper. I also plan to add a thumbnail bar with client selectors, complete with feedback and highlighting. I\'m building an auto-rotation timer with a visual progress bar, with pause on hover/touch, and play/pause toggle, and touch swipe and keyboard navigation. I\'m looking at using `AnimatePresence` for smooth transitions. I will also be looking into testing carousel logic.\n\n\n"
