  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s request, focusing intently on the annotated screenshot and their instruction to rename the \"SAIFULHERE\" H1 title within the landing hero section. I am breaking it down to be sure the directive is understood completely.\n\n\n**Refining Textual Specifications**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the specifications for the \"Saiful Islam\" rebranding within the hero section. I\'ve broken it into the brand elements, H1 text, and the subtitle below. I\'m focusing on the precise text, font, and brand guidelines to ensure accuracy. The brandmark is \'saifulhere,\' and I am thinking about how to render it using the provided specifications.\nI\'m also considering the font, style, and presentation.\n\n**Examining Testimonial Components**\n\nI\'m working through the new testimonial features. My focus is on integrating pictures, enhancing readability using a frosted glass panel with a light ash background, and ensuring the auto-review carousel remains active. I am also planning to find or make client portraits/photos for each testimonial author.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the visual upgrades for the testimonials. First, I need to source or create client portraits for Elena, Marcus, Dr. Sophia, Arthur, and Kareem. I\'ll check `/public/assets` and `/src/assets/images` for existing assets and plan to use `generate_image` if needed. I\'m also refining the frosted glass panel with a light ash background, aiming for a readable, sophisticated look using `bg-[#222326]/85` or similar tones, with a backdrop blur and crisp white text. Finally, the auto-review carousel will remain active without an easy toggle.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Scroll Interactions**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the scroll interactions. I want to enable a reading progress bar at the top, colored crimson, and implementing global smooth scrolling, plus adding section animations for the cinematic experience. My plan is to add a fixed reading progress bar to the top. I need a crimson color: and I will use smooth scroll.\n\n\n"
