ash-slate look, like `bg-[#232428]/80 backdrop-blur-2xl border border-white/20 shadow-[0_20px_50px_rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]`. I\'ll also add an internal card layer for improved contrast. I want to make sure it is perfect!\n\n\n**Implementing Progress Bar**\n\nI\'m now implementing a reading progress bar at the top of the viewport. I\'ll focus on making it subtle and effective in tracking the user\'s scroll position. I\'m aiming for a visually unobtrusive element that provides clear feedback on reading progress.\n\n\n**Creating Scroll Bar**\n\nI\'m building a smooth, crimson-colored scroll progress bar as a fixed element, styled for subtle tracking. I\'m leveraging `requestAnimationFrame` for responsive updates and considering React\'s `useScroll` with `useSpring` for ultra-smooth rendering. The progress is calculated dynamically to reflect user scroll position within the page.\n\n\n"
