  planner_response {
    response: "### What Was Done\n\n1. **Hero Headline & Company Branding Renamed**:\n   - Renamed the landing hero H1 heading to **`SAIFUL ISLAM`** as requested.\n   - Displayed the company brand name **`saifulhere`** in small lowercase monospace with a crimson accent dot (`saifulhere.studio \302\267 Principal Portfolio` in the hero, and `saifulhere.` in the header wordmark and footer) to match the cinematic noir aesthetic.\n\n2. **Testimonials with Pictures, Light Ash Frosted Panel & Readability**:\n   - **Client Photographs**: Integrated real portrait photos into both the active testimonial spotlight card and each thumbnail selector button.\n   - **Light Ash Frosted Glass Panel**: Redesigned the card with a light ash-tinted backdrop (`bg-gradient-to-br from-[#26282f]/95 via-[#202126]/95 to-[#191a1e]/95 backdrop-blur-2xl border border-white/20`), adding depth and visual separation from the background particle field.\n   - **Elevated Readability**: Increased quote contrast with crisp, high-legibility white typography (`text-white drop-shadow-sm`), clear `#d4d1cc` secondary metadata, and high-contrast badges.\n   - **Auto Review Always On**: Set the auto-rotation to continuous cycle mode with an active status beacon (`Auto [Always On]`), allowing manual navigation without killing the auto-scroll loop.\n\n3. **Subtle Crimson Reading Progress Bar**:\n   - Implemented a fixed reading progress bar at the very top of the viewport (`ScrollProgressBar.tsx`).\n   - Powered by spring physics (`motion/react` `useScroll` + `useSpring`) with neon crimson glow styling (`#e32b3c`) and a trailing light pip.\n\n4. **Cinematic Scroll Animations**:\n   - Added smooth native scroll physics (`html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }`).\n   - Wrapped page sections in cinematic scroll-reveal transitions (`motion.div` with subtle upward glide and viewport intersection triggers) for an editorial, smooth scrolling feel throughout the entire portfolio."
    modified_response: "### What Was Done\n\n1. **Hero Headline & Company Branding Renamed**:\n   - Renamed the landing hero H1 heading to **`SAIFUL ISLAM`** as requested.\n   - Displayed the company brand name **`saifulhere`** in small lowercase monospace with a crimson accent dot (`saifulhere.studio \302\267 Principal Portfolio` in the hero, and `saifulhere.` in the header wordmark and footer) to match the cinematic noir aesthetic.\n\n2. **Testimonials with Pictures, Light Ash Frosted Panel & Readability**:\n   - **Client Photographs**: Integrated real portrait photos into both the active testimonial spotlight card and each thumbnail selector button.\n   - **Light Ash Frosted Glass Panel**: Redesigned the card with a light ash-tinted backdrop (`bg-gradient-to-br from-[#26282f]/95 via-[#202126]/95 to-[#191a1e]/95 backdrop-blur-2xl border border-white/20`), adding depth and visual separation from the background particle field.\n   - **Elevated Readability**: Increased quote contrast with crisp, high-legibility white typography (`text-white drop-shadow-sm`), clear `#d4d1cc` secondary metadata, and high-contrast badges.\n   - **Auto Review Always On**: Set the auto-rotation to continuous cycle mode with an active status beacon (`Auto [Always On]`), allowing manual navigation without killing the auto-scroll loop.\n\n3. **Subtle Crimson Reading Progress Bar**:\n   - Implemented a fixed reading progress bar at the very top of the viewport (`ScrollProgressBar.tsx`).\n   - Powered by spring physics (`motion/react` `useScroll` + `useSpring`) with neon crimson glow styling (`#e32b3c`) and a trailing light pip.\n\n4. **Cinematic Scroll Animations**:\n   - Added smooth native scroll physics (`html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }`).\n   - Wrapped page sections in cinematic scroll-reveal transitions (`motion.div` with subtle upward glide and viewport intersection triggers) for an editorial, smooth scrolling feel throughout the entire portfolio."
