  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Configuration Mismatch**\n\nI\'m noticing a discrepancy in port configurations. The application environment shows `PORT: 8080`, but the control plane seems to be listening on port 8000. I also saw this in `process.env.PORT` vs control plane expectations. `ps aux` confirms the control plane is using `--listen-addr=:8000`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Port Assignment**\n\nI\'ve got it! The issue was the `process.env.PORT` override.  It was set to 8080 by the subshell or the Cloud Run container.  My `server.ts` file correctly interpreted this when `parseInt(process.env.PORT || \'3000\', 10)` executed, causing the server to listen on port 8080. This was a mismatch because nginx and the AI Studio dev proxy was forwarding traffic to the expected port 3000, where nothing was listening.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Port Configuration**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the port configuration logic. I see we have a few options: a CLI argument `--port`, a default of 3000, and potentially `process.env.PORT`. The system prompt\'s environment constraint specifically mandates port 3000.  The crucial part is prioritizing the `--port` argument, if present, over the environment variable and default. This prioritizes the environment\'s specified value.\n\n\n"
