  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Port Conflicts**\n\nI\'ve discovered that nginx is occupying port 8080, and node is running on 3000. It seems setting `process.env.PORT` or the `PORT` environment variable to 8080 caused server.ts to attempt to bind to the same port as nginx, which leads to `EADDRINUSE` errors.\n\n\n**Confirming Port Binding Logic**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the `EADDRINUSE` error stems from the server attempting to bind to port 8080, already occupied by nginx. It seems the issue lies in the server\'s port configuration, specifically the fallback to `process.env.PORT`. The recent code refactoring resolves this by ensuring the application always listens on port 3000 unless a `--port` argument is given, preventing future port conflicts by default.\n\n\n"
